"'''What Makes You Beautiful'''" (often abbreviated as '''WMYB''') is the debut single by the British-Irish boy band [[One Direction]]. It was the lead single from their debut album, ''[[Up All Night (One Direction album)|Up All Night]]'' (2011). Written by [[Savan Kotecha]] and producer [[Rami Yacoub]], the song was released by [[Syco Records]] on 11 September 2011. The uptempo [[power pop]]<ref name=Powerpop/> track features a prominent guitar-based chorus and [[riff]]. The [[middle eight]] consists of a "na na na" [[hook (music)|hook]].

"What Makes You Beautiful" was a commercial success, reaching number one in several countries. It has been certified quadruple platinum in the US with sales of 4.8 million copies as of June 2016.<ref name="USsales2016"/> The single peaked at number four on the US [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] and number one on the [[UK Singles Chart]]. The song won the [[2012 Brit Awards|2012]] [[Brit Award for British Single of the Year]] and was generally complimented by contemporary [[Music journalism|music critics]], who highlighted the appeal to the teenage audience and the pop sensibility. It debuted at number one on the UK Singles Chart after setting a [[Sony Music Entertainment]] pre-order record and selling 153,965 copies in its first week. The single topped the [[Irish Singles Chart|Irish]] and [[Scottish Singles and Albums Charts|Scottish]] Singles Charts, and reached the top ten on the [[ARIA Charts|Australian]] and [[Recording Industry Association of New Zealand|New Zealand]] Singles Charts, Flemish [[Ultratop 50]], [[Canadian Hot 100]], and the [[Japan Hot 100]].

The song's accompanying music video, directed by John Urbano, was uploaded to [[YouTube]] on 19 August 2011. It depicts One Direction spending time on a beach in [[Malibu, California]]. The video garnered three [[MTV Video Music Awards]] at the [[2012 MTV Video Music Awards|2012 ceremony]]. One Direction performed the song live on televised shows, at awards ceremonies, and on all four of their headlining concert tours: [[Up All Night Tour]] (2011–12), [[Take Me Home Tour (One Direction)|Take Me Home Tour]] (2013), [[Where We Are Tour (One Direction)|Where We Are Tour]] (2014), and [[On the Road Again Tour]] (2015); band member [[Harry Styles]] performed the song on his [[Harry Styles: Live on Tour|2017]] and [[Love On Tour|2021 solo tours]]. Many artists have [[Cover version|covered]] the song, including [[the Piano Guys]], [[Boyce Avenue]], and [[Enhypen]]. It is often regarded as One Direction's signature song, and one of the most iconic and recognisable pop songs of the 2010s.

